    "readme_description": "Given an `m x n` matrix `board` where each cell is a battleship `'X'` or empty `'.'`, return the number of the battleships on `board`.\n\nBattleships can only be placed horizontally or vertically on `board`. In other words, they can only be made of the shape `1 x k` (`1` row, `k` columns) or `k x 1` (`k` rows, `1` column), where `k` can be of any size. At least one horizontal or vertical cell separates between two battleships (i.e., there are no adjacent battleships).",
    "_readme_examples": {
        "list": [
            {
                "content": "![Example 1](https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2024/06/21/image.png)\n\n```\nInput: board = [[\"X\",\".\",\".\",\"X\"],[\".\",\".\",\".\",\"X\"],[\".\",\".\",\".\",\"X\"]]\nOutput: 2\n```"
            },
            {
                "content": "```\nInput: board = [[\".\"]]\nOutput: 0\n```"
            }
        ]
    },
    "readme_constraints": "- m == board.length\n- n == board[i].length\n- 1 <= m, n <= 200\n- board[i][j] is either '.' or 'X'.\n\nFollow up: Could you do it in one-pass, using only O(1) extra memory and without modifying the values of board?",
